# 🔍 AB Talks AI Challenge – Day 14

## Topic: Semantic Search with Vector Databases

### Problem Statement

Traditional keyword search only finds documents containing the exact query words.

Semantic search goes beyond keywords by understanding the meaning and intent behind a query. It uses embeddings and vector similarity search to retrieve relevant documents even when different words are used.

In this project, we build a semantic search engine using OpenAI Embeddings and FAISS, then compare its performance with traditional keyword search.

